Use this form only after establishing that the instrument requires mutual consent to end, or that
both parties want the record closed. Many agreements give one side a unilateral termination right,
and an indefinite agreement may be terminable on notice — in those cases the board authorizes the
entity to exercise its own right and this form is unnecessary. A board resolution can never, by
itself, release the counterparty's rights. Both parties sign this one, each in every capacity engaged.

**The release in ¶3 is a separate bargain, not part of terminating.** Delete it, or narrow it, unless
counsel has identified what is being given up.

**1. Status of the instrument.** As of the date of this agreement:

   - amount advanced or drawn to date: **$<AMOUNT — state $0 if none>**
   - principal outstanding: **$<AMOUNT>**
   - interest accrued and unpaid: **$<AMOUNT>**
   - other amounts owing under it: **$<AMOUNT>**
   - performance rendered by either party under it: <DESCRIBE, or "none">

*(If the instrument was never operated, say so plainly here rather than leaving the reader to infer
it from four zeroes.)*

**2. Termination.** The instrument is terminated in its entirety, effective on the date of this
agreement. It is not terminated retroactively, and nothing here states that it was ineffective
before today.

**3. Mutual release.** *(optional — include only on counsel's advice)* Each party releases the other
from claims arising under or in connection with the instrument, **other than**: claims for fraud or
intentional misconduct; indemnification and contribution rights; confidentiality obligations; rights
in any collateral or guaranty; accrued and unpaid amounts; tax obligations of either party; and
<ANY OTHER CARVE-OUT>. Surviving provisions of the instrument remain in force: <LIST, or "none">.

**4. Originals.** The original instrument and any note or other negotiable document executed with it
are marked "CANCELLED" and retained in the Entity's records at <LOCATION>. <Originals not in the
Entity's possession are to be obtained from <HOLDER> and cancelled; until then this agreement is the
Entity's evidence of termination.>

**5. Tax treatment.** The parties record that <no amount is forgiven and no cancellation-of-
indebtedness income arises / the following amount is forgiven and its treatment has been referred to
the parties' tax advisers: $<AMOUNT>>. Each party relies on its own adviser.

**6. No other change.** No other agreement between the parties is amended by this agreement.

